title: "3D Chromatin Organization in CNS Neurons: Hi-C Data Analysis Across Developmental and Injury States"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-01-01

authors:
  - family-names: "[Last Name]"
    given-names: "[First Name]"
    affiliation: "[Your Institution]"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX"   # optional

repository-code: "https://github.com/<your-username>/<repo-name>"
license: MIT

abstract: >
  A comprehensive computational pipeline for analyzing three-dimensional chromatin
  organization in CNS neurons using Hi-C sequencing data. The pipeline covers
  A/B compartment analysis, TAD calling, chromatin loop calling, and pairwise
  differential comparison across developmental stages (E12.5, P0, Adult) and
  neuronal injury conditions. Built on HOMER with custom R scripts for annotation
  and visualization.

keywords:
  - Hi-C
  - 3D genome
  - chromatin organization
  - TAD
  - chromatin loops
  - A/B compartments
  - CNS neurons
  - neuronal development
  - neuronal injury
  - bioinformatics
  - mm10
  - HOMER
